        <item>
            <title>3.27.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:22:56 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>242</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.27.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's New in 3.27.0</h2><ul></ul><p><strong>New</strong></p><ul><li>Right-click a folder in Finder and choose Rename with Zush to rename the files inside it. Files in subfolders stay as they are.</li><li>See and edit each file's Finder tags in the file list before you rename.</li></ul><p><strong>Improved</strong></p><ul><li>Cloud AI analysis is faster, and a slow reply switches to a backup service sooner.</li><li>Large batches of videos use less memory.</li><li>Rename &amp; sort keeps the list grouped by folder while files are renamed.</li><li>Activation errors are clearer, and Zush asks you to check your internet connection only when the connection is the problem.</li><li>More of the app is translated, including privacy prompts, icon tooltips and color names.</li></ul><p><strong>Fixed</strong></p><ul><li>Undo All no longer lists files it has already put back.</li><li>Names with extensions such as .tar.gz keep the full extension when the name is already taken.</li><li>Tags and descriptions now reach files that were renamed while Zush was still reading them, and tags you edited stay.</li><li>Folder monitoring tries interrupted sorting again instead of reporting it as failed.</li><li>Fixed a crash when reading location data from some videos.</li></ul>
]]></description>
